            "text": "The FBI's own surveillance network has been compromised by Chinese government-affiliated hackers. FISA warrant data. Call records. IP addresses. The system that tracks suspected foreign agents - now observed by the very people it was designed to monitor. The irony writes itself, but the implications don't. This follows Salt Typhoon (2024-2025), when Chinese actors breached [HANDLE_REDACTED] , AT&T, and Lumen - the telecom carriers that enable government surveillance. The pattern: systematically map and compromise your adversary's intelligence infrastructure. Know what they know about you. For UK organisations, the lesson is stark. If the FBI's internal systems aren't immune, yours aren't either. The question isn't whether a nation-state actor can get in. It's whether you'd notice them once they're there. #Cybersecurity #ThreatIntel #Espionage #NationalSecurity."
